# Cloudflare Pages reads this file and applies the headers to matching paths.
#
# The game is served from whichanimaltoday.com and fetches its data from here,
# which is a different origin — so without this header the browser blocks every
# request and the game shows its error card to everyone at once.
#
# This is not a new requirement introduced by Cloudflare. It is what
# raw.githubusercontent.com was already sending; verified 2026-08-07:
#   access-control-allow-origin: *
# Migrating without it silently removes something the site depends on.
#
# `*` is correct here. These files are public data, already readable by anyone
# with the URL, and restricting the origin would only break the Framer preview
# domain and any future custom domain.
/*
  Access-Control-Allow-Origin: *
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=300

